        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c9966b13-42f8-52f2-92e0-fbdec2870ea8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William McKinley\n- Laws: McKinley Tariff, Tariff Act of 1890\n- Organizations: United States Congress, Republican Party\n- Events: United States elections of 1890, Panic of 1890\n- Roles: President of the United States, U.S. Representative\n\nFacts:\n- William McKinley framed the Tariff Act of 1890 in his role as a U.S. Representative.\n- The Tariff Act of 1890, commonly called the McKinley Tariff, became law on October 1, 1890.\n- In the United States elections of 1890, the Republican Party suffered major losses because of the Panic of 1890 and the unpopularity of the McKinley Tariff.\n- William McKinley served as the 25th President of the United States from March 4, 1897 until his assassination in September 1901, six months into his second term.",
